{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1499965-ways-to-make-a-wraith-threatening","id":1499965,"title":"Ways to make a Wraith Threatening","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-12-17T13:26:38-08:00","id":1499965,"title":"Ways to make a Wraith Threatening","content":"Well, I decided to create this topic here instead of the Wraith's subforum because the Wraith's subforum is a bit dead (no pun intended lol).<br /> <br /> So, one thing that has always bothered me is that Wraith's were never taken seriously as a threat by players in general in all my years of experience with the setting, unlike Mages and Werewolves (understandably because of the powercreep often present in those splats). While I have a great deal of knowledge about Mages, Vampires and Werewolves, I admittedly don't have much knowledge about Wraiths. So, besides the fact that Wraiths are not well known for their powers, in this I mean they're not known as potentially broken as Mages, Vampires and Werewolves can be, I know next to nothing about their powers. Then, my question is: is it possible to make Wraiths really dangerous to the other splats in terms of powers? Do they have powers that could really threaten the other splats besides scaring them? I mean that not only in a narrative sense, because that's another thing, I mean really in their arsenal of powers etc. How can I make a Wraith threatening to the players so that they learn to stop thinking they can just &quot;summon and compel any Wraith to do as they please at any time&quot; (in case they're Giovanni, Cappadocian, etc.) or just outright ignore them? Btw, I have W20, so that if you have any suggestion of where to find information regarding their powers in the book, that would be also very helpful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-17T14:45:02-08:00","id":1499969,"title":"","content":"Well first, if it's Vampire PCs, they can only see a Wraith if they have Auspex 2 (Aura Reading) or a specific Necromancy power. So, by default, Wraiths are invisible to vampire characters. Same with Mages who don't have Spirit 1. And if the character has no way to see the Wraith, they probably also lack the ability to directly hurt them, too. Any discussion of how threatening Wraiths are must begin with the assumption that they cannot be seen or touched by most characters.<br /> <br /> Now, Wraiths generally lack the ability to touch mortals in kind, but they're more likely to have powers that can circumvent the barrier and affect the material world. After all, if they had no such powers, they probably wouldn't be relevant to proceedings this side of the Shroud.<br /> <br /> Werewolves are a different matter, obviously, as Wraiths are <i>kind of</i> spirits in the Garou sense. Those more versed in Werewolf know better than I do. Just know that the ability to translate into the Middle Umbra (aka &quot;Spirit Wilds&quot;) is not the same as the power to translate into the Low (Dark) Umbra. Garou characters can't necessarily follow the ghosts to where they &quot;live&quot;. I assume.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-17T15:10:40-08:00","id":1499973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1499965-ways-to-make-a-wraith-threatening?p=1499969#post1499969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well first, if it's Vampire PCs, they can only see a Wraith if they have Auspex 2 (Aura Reading) or a specific Necromancy power. So, by default, Wraiths are invisible to vampire characters. Same with Mages who don't have Spirit 1. And if the character has no way to see the Wraith, they probably also lack the ability to directly hurt them, too. Any discussion of how threatening Wraiths are must begin with the assumption that they cannot be seen or touched by most characters.<br /> <br /> Now, Wraiths generally lack the ability to touch mortals in kind, but they're more likely to have powers that can circumvent the barrier and affect the material world. After all, if they had no such powers, they probably wouldn't be relevant to proceedings this side of the Shroud.<br /> <br /> Werewolves are a different matter, obviously, as Wraiths are <i>kind of</i> spirits in the Garou sense. Those more versed in Werewolf know better than I do. Just know that the ability to translate into the Middle Umbra (aka &quot;Spirit Wilds&quot;) is not the same as the power to translate into the Low (Dark) Umbra. Garou characters can't necessarily follow the ghosts to where they &quot;live&quot;. I assume.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I understand all of these points, the thing I'm asking here is exactly how they can really affect the world this side of the Shroud. Likewise, I'm more interested in their powers to deal with a group of PCs if they happen to make a Wraith enemy, for instance. The thing is, besides the suggested stats to &quot;translate&quot; their powers into vampire or another splat system of powers (that are, for the most part, terrible), I don't know their powers well enough to make them a real threat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-17T15:15:46-08:00","id":1499975,"title":"","content":"With regards to the Arcanoi, a number of them are usable in the Skinlands. For example the primary nature of Inhabit is to possess objects and machines. In Wr20 Inhabit 1 grains a wraith the ability to possess an object, Inhabit 2 allows them to cause that device to temporarily malfunction and Inhabit 3 allows them to control it. With could be a serious problem for a group of vampires at the wrong moment. Oh you're trying to drive somewhere? Suddenly you car fails. Or you lose control of it and it races into an intersection during a red light.<br /> <br /> There's also the possibility that a wraith might have a Passion somehow connected one of the vampires which could result in them being a reoccurring headache for them. After all, if you got killed by a vampire and ended up as a wraith, there would be a good chance that you'd want to make that vampire's life miserable.<br /> <br /> Then there's the ability of a wraith to become risen which can be much more directly dangerous, especially if again that wraith is out for blood against a member of the coterie as becoming a risen is difficult and many of those that do become risen are really, <b><i>really</i></b> motivated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-17T15:23:58-08:00","id":1499976,"title":"","content":"Outrage can light vampires on fire while they sleep...and Flux can turn a haven into a deathtrap. Inhabit can get the vampire SWATed. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-17T15:37:46-08:00","id":1499982,"title":"","content":"Thank you for the suggestions, what interests me the most are the powers that can affect the Skinlands, I'm interested in knowing where to look for information regarding these as at the moment I can't read the entire W20 and prepare a story at the same time, I'm quite busy. I'll have a look at these powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-17T15:39:40-08:00","id":1499983,"title":"","content":"By the way, Risen is a fascinating concept. I'll look for more information about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-17T15:41:48-08:00","id":1499984,"title":"","content":"I have had the best luck when using Wraiths as indirect threats rather than a standup fight sort of threat.<br /> <br /> Sticking with vampire &amp; ghost interactions for simplicity, most vampires can't perceive the ghosts and the few disciplines that allow it generally aren't left constantly running with the characters constantly scanning their surroundings. Thus the ghost is the ears and eyes in every room, did the PCs just make a cool plan to defeat the necromancer, well too bad the ghosts just revealed it all to its master.<br /> <br /> More importantly you have to remember that ghosts don't have the same daylight restriction that vampires do. Thus a ghost can wander into any haven at mid-day and look around. Now that might not sound like much of a threat, but consider how many things laying around your house that can be dangerous with only tiny amounts of manipulation. Starting fires, opening water taps, pulling back a window blind, etc can all be done, depending on the ghosts given load out. None of these things will directly harm a vampire, but it can create situations where the vampire is put in significantly greater danger.<br /> <br /> In simpler terms, ghosts are kind of like fighting a streak of super bad luck. Trying pull off a heist in a getaway car, well it seems a couple of spark plug wires disconnected and stopped the car from running. Are you trying to sell a load of weapons to a gang, how did a hand grenade pin pop out on its own? Trying to hack the company files of a rival kindred, well your breakers keep tripping or there is a power surge that kills the computer.<br /> <br /> Using ghosts to terrify the Players is more about understanding what tiny things in the mundane world can go wrong than knowing the ins and outs of Wraith rules. A new ghost probably can't telekinetically punch a vampire or throw them across the room, but they can tip a cup of coffee over to short out the laptop they are working with.<br /> <br /> The best part is that unless the ghost or the necromancer makes a big display of their power, no one will have any idea what is going on or who is behind it. To use a Warhammer 40k reference, having a ghost as an enemy turns the PCs into Lamenter space marines crossed with the Afriel strain guardsmen clones. If it can go wrong, it will and in spades.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-17T16:45:25-08:00","id":1499991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Using ghosts to terrify the Players is more about understanding what tiny things in the mundane world can go wrong than knowing the ins and outs of Wraith rules. A new ghost probably can't telekinetically punch a vampire or throw them across the room, but they can tip a cup of coffee over to short out the laptop they are working with. </div> </div> </div>True, but at the same time, as I mentioned earlier, in general these are things that any ST with some experience will know. I'm actually interested in knowing what Wraith's are capable of doing, etc. Changelings, Mages, Vampires and Werewolves all have a wide variety of powers, some of which are quite impressive. The thing is I don't know enough of Wraiths to have a good idea of what they are capable of doing, unlike the other splats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-17T19:05:14-08:00","id":1500001,"title":"","content":"Making them terrifying isn't the problem. If anything, it's that they have too great an ability to zip past player defenses and casually assassinate them. I use a heavily nerfed version of wraiths, keeping them as mainly useful spies. Any time you have an opponent who can zip past defenses and attack from nowhere, it's a problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-17T20:28:17-08:00","id":1500005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1499965-ways-to-make-a-wraith-threatening?p=1499982#post1499982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you for the suggestions, what interests me the most are the powers that can affect the Skinlands, I'm interested in knowing where to look for information regarding these as at the moment I can't read the entire W20 and prepare a story at the same time, I'm quite busy. I'll have a look at these powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Arcanoi are the powers of wraiths just as Disciplines are for vampires. There's a whole section on them in the Traits Chapter of Wr20.<br /> <br /> As for the Risen, Chapter 11 of Wr20 is dedicated to the Risen.<br /> <br /> And if you want to give a lifeline to your players in dealing with ghosts without them getting tangled up with the Giovanni, Wr20 has an appendix chapter dedicated to Orpheus, the spiritual successor to WtO that deals with the Orpheus Group, a company that deals with ghosts.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-18T00:46:50-08:00","id":1500019,"title":"","content":"It's generally worth remembering that Wraiths are spirits, after a fashion. Ergo, you could always use the Charms of spirits from Werewolf, if you need mechanics for the kinds of powers they can manifest in meatspace.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-18T06:39:27-08:00","id":1500032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1499965-ways-to-make-a-wraith-threatening?p=1499991#post1499991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True, but at the same time, as I mentioned earlier, in general these are things that any ST with some experience will know. I'm actually interested in knowing what Wraith's are capable of doing, etc. Changelings, Mages, Vampires and Werewolves all have a wide variety of powers, some of which are quite impressive. The thing is I don't know enough of Wraiths to have a good idea of what they are capable of doing, unlike the other splats.</div> </div> </div> </div>An experienced ST would either read the condensed splat version in the V:tM book (pages 384-386 in V20) or read the actual Wraith book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-18T06:42:40-08:00","id":1500033,"title":"","content":"I mean....this is a pretty decent breakdown: <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Arcanos_(WTO)\" target=\"_blank\">Arcanos (WTO) | White Wolf Wiki | Fandom</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-18T09:25:27-08:00","id":1500046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1499965-ways-to-make-a-wraith-threatening?p=1500032#post1500032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> An experienced ST would either read the condensed splat version in the V:tM book (pages 384-386 in V20) or read the actual Wraith book.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm curious to understand what you meant by that, really, because of course I've read the condensed splat version and at the same time it's not hard to imagine an experienced ST who haven't read much about Wraiths. But, in any case, that isn't what I asked here If you don't have anything useful to say, just don't join the discussion. Acting like a &quot;you know what&quot; isn't going to make you look better and isn't helpful to anyone. Just learn to respect other people and leave this thread, that's the best you can do. Because what you're doing just discourage people from having interesting discussions where useful information can often be shared. If you're unhappy about your life or anything, don't take it out on other people, ok?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12348,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","user":"Herr Meister","date":". 12-18-2022, 12:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-19T07:35:48-08:00","id":1500096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1499965-ways-to-make-a-wraith-threatening?p=1500046#post1500046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious to understand what you meant by that, really, because of course I've read the condensed splat version and at the same time it's not hard to imagine an experienced ST who haven't read much about Wraiths. But, in any case, that isn't what I asked here If you don't have anything useful to say, just don't join the discussion. Acting like a &quot;you know what&quot; isn't going to make you look better and isn't helpful to anyone. Just learn to respect other people and leave this thread, that's the best you can do. Because what you're doing just discourage people from having interesting discussions where useful information can often be shared. If you're unhappy about your life or anything, don't take it out on other people, ok?</div> </div> </div> </div>You are asking the forum to summarize several splat lines worth of RAW mechanics into a central information packet, rather than doing the leg work on your own. It is one thing to ask about esoteric mechanical interactions, rare fluff quotes, or just asking where to start on a given topic. But it is something else to ask for a multi-system break down and then complain that people aren't giving you what you wanted.<br /> <br /> If you have read the condensed version, then as an experienced ST you have everything you need to make a story work. If you want more, then dive deeper into the books. By your own admission the Wraith forums are dead and you came to the VtM forums where many just use the simplified rules from the core book regarding ghosts. Beyond being told storytelling methods to use that simple rule set, what were you expecting?<br /> <br /> You aren't really asking for help; you are asking someone to do the leg work for you. Not much to respect in that sort of behavior, so don't act like a victim when someone calls you out on being lazy.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-19T11:06:59-08:00","id":1500107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1499965-ways-to-make-a-wraith-threatening?p=1500096#post1500096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You are asking the forum to summarize several splat lines worth of RAW mechanics into a central information packet, rather than doing the leg work on your own. It is one thing to ask about esoteric mechanical interactions, rare fluff quotes, or just asking where to start on a given topic. But it is something else to ask for a multi-system break down and then complain that people aren't giving you what you wanted.<br /> <br /> If you have read the condensed version, then as an experienced ST you have everything you need to make a story work. If you want more, then dive deeper into the books. By your own admission the Wraith forums are dead and you came to the VtM forums where many just use the simplified rules from the core book regarding ghosts. Beyond being told storytelling methods to use that simple rule set, what were you expecting?<br /> <br /> You aren't really asking for help; you are asking someone to do the leg work for you. Not much to respect in that sort of behavior, so don't act like a victim when someone calls you out on being lazy.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, I haven't asked for a &quot;multi-system break down&quot; of any sort, nor am I complaining about anything (besides bad manners <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />). I'm just more interested in the possible interaction of powers, especially because I'm thinking about a story where this might be really relevant. So, all in all I was more interested in the ways their powers work within the perspective of different storytelling method ideas. In fact, perhaps the main reason that made me create the topic is that players who make Giovanni characters or Telyavelic Tremere (or really any kind of necromancer) often act as if their necromantic powers means they have access to an unlimited source of ghosts who can provide them with information and are both easy to summon and/or control and are easy to get rid of. Sometimes this annoys me, when I see stories around many tables where this pattern repeat itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-19T11:38:53-08:00","id":1500112,"title":"","content":"Off the top of my head;<ul><li>Neutralize Celerity</li> <li>Counter Dominate (if somebody under the control of dominate is possessed by a wraith then the domitor and the wraith have a battle of wills for control of the person)</li> <li>Steal your blood pool.</li> <li>Make blood rot before you can eat it, effectively starving you.</li> <li>Send you into frenzy without warning. If you try to ride the wave, they can drag you out of it.</li> <li>Mess up your plans by possessing your thralls. Or murdering them. Or driving them insane.</li> <li>Edit and erase memories. Dominate is all fun and games until somebody starts using effects like that on you and your toys.</li> <li>Possess you. (Don't remember exactly if Wr20 addressed skinriding and torpor, but V5 has the possibility of wraiths possessing vampires while they daysleep and almost walking them into the sunlight.)</li> <li>Set fire to your haven, your domain, your businesses, your car, your hair and clothes, etc</li> <li>Give you horrific nightmares that make daysleep undesirable.</li> <li>Pick up an object with which to decapitate you, stake you, etc</li> <li>Drop kick you straight into Oblivion (Final Death, no coming back. Bye.)</li> <li>Read your entire browser history and message archives (and so on). Eavesdrop on your phone calls. Possibly send them to somebody you really don't want to know about the contents.</li> <li>Did you have important data that was crucial to your plans or would lead to terrible consequences if you acted upon this data not knowing certain details or believing lies? Well now it's been edited, or deleted to make you do so.</li> <li>I'm pretty sure making doors and entrances disappear is a thing.</li> <li>Spacial loops. Your own haven can become a maze, trapping you inside and unable to get out.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-19T11:57:48-08:00","id":1500114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1499965-ways-to-make-a-wraith-threatening?p=1500107#post1500107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, all in all I was more interested in the ways their powers work within the perspective of different storytelling method ideas. In fact, perhaps the main reason that made me create the topic is that players who make Giovanni characters or Telyavelic Tremere (or really any kind of necromancer) often act as if their necromantic powers means they have access to an unlimited source of ghosts who can provide them with information and are both easy to summon and/or control and are easy to get rid of. Sometimes this annoys me, when I see stories around many tables where this pattern repeat itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Patterns in storytelling is an occupational hazard if you go by <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Seven_Basic_Plots\" target=\"_blank\">The Seven Basic Plots</a>. All you can really do is try to disguise which ever plot you are using.<br /> <br /> As far as the mechanics interactions go... part of the problem is that many mechanics are made for balance rather than storytelling. For example, let's say a Necromancer wanted to make a ring they always wore a fetish for their most powerful ghost minions to allow for easy contact and access. The mechanics say each ghost costs one permanent willpower to bind. This sounds fine until you realize that if you have anything but low-level willpower, this gets prohibitively expensive in terms of XP costs. So, the only Necromancers who can regularly make fetishes are those with the weakest wills regardless of their necromantic proficiency. Even if you rule that each ghost needs their own fetish rather than a shared one, the cost ends up being the same.<br /> <br /> So being overly attached to exact mechanics interactions are not always beneficial to the storytelling process.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-19T12:44:55-08:00","id":1500121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Patterns in storytelling is an occupational hazard if you go by <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Seven_Basic_Plots\" target=\"_blank\">The Seven Basic Plots</a>. All you can really do is try to disguise which ever plot you are using. </div> </div> </div>This is a really interesting book that I definitely need to read. I have yet to read the book, but my impression is that an RPG Chronicle rarely fits into only one of these &quot;plots&quot; and I also wonder if Game of Thrones would be considered a Tragedy by this classification. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So being overly attached to exact mechanics interactions are not always beneficial to the storytelling process. </div> </div> </div>While I certainly agree with that, I know from experience that to only know or even to limit the other splats in the game to their &quot;simplified version&quot; present at each of the own splat's books limit the true potential of these said splats. So, let's take how vampires are described in Werewolf books, in the &quot;translated&quot; character sheet, they don't get nearly a 10% of their true potential. It's as if it was a completely different creature compared to when you create the character with its traits and powers based on the own splat's book. Perhaps Werewolf is the worst example, because it's really hard to translate other powers such as Disciplines and Spheres to Gifts, most of the time this translation severely limit the potential of the vampire or mage. Of course, I'm aware that this is not really that important when you think about storytelling, but that is something that can nonetheless be of help when fleshing out a character from another splat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-19T12:55:28-08:00","id":1500124,"title":"","content":"Wraiths can be very potent across the Shroud since it is their home turf. More than just being individually powerful, it's their sheer numbers and organization of groups like the Hierarchy that have enormous resources. A vampire crossing the Shroud and entering the Shadowlands in most Necropoli better be discrete and on good behavior because the ST can throw a lot at them.<br /> <br /> Wraiths are much more constrained in the Skinlands because either their powers don't work, require an area where the Shroud is thin, or face other limitations. That doesn't mean they can't harass or even threaten others, just that it is rare. You can build a very strong character who can do a lot across the Shroud and load them with relics and artifacts, but those should be very rare and exceptional characters.<br /> <br /> If you are looking for a straight character versus character fight (wraith versus any non-wraith like a vampire, werewolf, etc.), I think that would be a mistake. It is not a good emulation of ghost stories which is what most players would want. If I wanted to run one or more scenes showing a terrifying encounter with Wraiths, I'd look to the best kinds of ghost stories that deal with people feeling physically threatened by ghosts - Blatty's The Exorcist, Matheson's Hell House, the Poltergeist movie, or the ghost stories of M.R. James - and try to emulate one of them.<br /> <br /> The initial tendency of many STs is to want to do one-on-one fights between splats, but in practice almost the best thing for any splat to do is avoid a one-on-one fight and utilize the natural advantages they have against the other splay and wage asymmetric warfare. If a wraith needs to fight vampires, he doesn't haunt them directly. He possesses someone in the Skinlands during the day and helps hunters locate the vampire's haven. He haunts the people in someone's Herds so they flee or commit suicide. He causes a car accident that kills someone's ghoul. He lures them into a haunted house at night where they don't encounter that wraith, but an entire circle of Renegades or Spectres angry at being disturbed. Torment them with sounds and fleeting sights at odd times and places in the night so they're never quite sure what is going on, and that may cause them to make a crucial mistake like run into a Sabbat pack, stay out too long and not able to safely hide before the sun comes up, or wander into a rival's domain.<br /> <br /> My general advice to most STs who want to include wraiths in their games, but don't have the material or time to master an entirely different gameline is just do their best to emulate the popular ghost stories they know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-19T13:25:58-08:00","id":1500130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1499965-ways-to-make-a-wraith-threatening?p=1500124#post1500124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wraiths can be very potent across the Shroud since it is their home turf. More than just being individually powerful, it's their sheer numbers and organization of groups like the Hierarchy that have enormous resources. A vampire crossing the Shroud and entering the Shadowlands in most Necropoli better be discrete and on good behavior because the ST can throw a lot at them.<br /> <br /> Wraiths are much more constrained in the Skinlands because either their powers don't work, require an area where the Shroud is thin, or face other limitations. That doesn't mean they can't harass or even threaten others, just that it is rare. You can build a very strong character who can do a lot across the Shroud and load them with relics and artifacts, but those should be very rare and exceptional characters.<br /> <br /> If you are looking for a straight character versus character fight (wraith versus any non-wraith like a vampire, werewolf, etc.), I think that would be a mistake. It is not a good emulation of ghost stories which is what most players would want. If I wanted to run one or more scenes showing a terrifying encounter with Wraiths, I'd look to the best kinds of ghost stories that deal with people feeling physically threatened by ghosts - Blatty's The Exorcist, Matheson's Hell House, the Poltergeist movie, or the ghost stories of M.R. James - and try to emulate one of them.<br /> <br /> The initial tendency of many STs is to want to do one-on-one fights between splats, but in practice almost the best thing for any splat to do is avoid a one-on-one fight and utilize the natural advantages they have against the other splay and wage asymmetric warfare. If a wraith needs to fight vampires, he doesn't haunt them directly. He possesses someone in the Skinlands during the day and helps hunters locate the vampire's haven. He haunts the people in someone's Herds so they flee or commit suicide. He causes a car accident that kills someone's ghoul. He lures them into a haunted house at night where they don't encounter that wraith, but an entire circle of Renegades or Spectres angry at being disturbed. Torment them with sounds and fleeting sights at odd times and places in the night so they're never quite sure what is going on, and that may cause them to make a crucial mistake like run into a Sabbat pack, stay out too long and not able to safely hide before the sun comes up, or wander into a rival's domain.<br /> <br /> My general advice to most STs who want to include wraiths in their games, but don't have the material or time to master an entirely different gameline is just do their best to emulate the popular ghost stories they know.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Very interesting! Thank you for your input!<br /> <br /> Btw, I love both Bly Manor and Hill House from Mike Flanagan, even though I probably prefer Bly Manor, both are very interesting stories to draw inspiration from. And yes, the way RPGs work, lead us to straight one-on-one fights, especially because many players like that, in the way that familiarity brings some comfort, but especially in this case scenario, I agree that it's by far not the best approach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12348,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","user":"Herr Meister","date":". 12-19-2022, 06:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-19T15:14:25-08:00","id":1500140,"title":"","content":"A couple of things to to remember if your Necromancers are abusing wreaths too much:<br /> <br /> - Wraiths have Circle Mates and most Necromancers powers are one on one, so whilde vampy isabsolutely safe from that one ghost the rest of them are free to pummel, flambe, possess and rupture him to their hearts content.<br /> <br /> - one of the easiest ways to control a Wraiths is to threaten one of their Fetters but it is a dangerous game of chicken as destroying the Fetter will send said wraith into a Harrowing they are by no means a one way trip and when said wraith returns they will be incredibly angry, no longer under control and likely getting a bunch of assistance f4om their Shadow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-19T22:58:07-08:00","id":1500165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1499965-ways-to-make-a-wraith-threatening#post1499965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How can I make a Wraith threatening to the players so that they learn to stop thinking they can just &quot;summon and compel any Wraith to do as they please at any time&quot; (in case they're Giovanni, Cappadocian, etc.) or just outright ignore them?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1499965-ways-to-make-a-wraith-threatening?p=1500130#post1500130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yes, the way RPGs work, lead us to straight one-on-one fights, especially because many players like that, in the way that familiarity brings some comfort, but especially in this case scenario, I agree that it's by far not the best approach.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you are looking for individual scenes that can get across to certain PCs that their powers do not make them immune, here are some examples of the kind of scenes I'd do.<br /> <br /> 1) Wraiths can invade your dreams and manipulate them (the Phantasm Arcanos). I would not go full Freddy Krueger, but I would use that as opportunity for wraiths to communicate to a vampire (who is slumbering in the daytime) in a safe environment for all sides. If you want to impress upon the vampire their power, you could have the Hierarchy hold a mock trial of the vampire for their crimes against wraiths. No powers are on either side can be used against each other, but you could show a lot of wraiths in a Star Chamber style court, wraiths in the jury, wraiths as bailiffs, etc. to showcase their numbers and resources. End the scene in a way that clearly (and hopefully ominously) warns the PC.<br /> <br /> 2) You can start the scene whenever the PC is driving somewhere. Describe that as they look in their rear view mirror they see someone smiling at them in their backseat. There is no one in the back seat of course, the mirror is simply showing the wraith (through the Embody Arcanos). If they turn their head and look back, they see nothing. But regardless their car suddenly jerks and it crashes (through either the Inhabit or Outrage Arcanoi). <br /> <br /> 3) When the vampire awakes, he finds out his haven is destroyed by a fire. Maybe he is in the basement and survived the flames. Maybe a retainer managed to move his resting spot to a new haven which he wakes up in. Maybe he awakens as the flames are erupting at sunset. But whether it is through some kind of spontaneous combustion or faulty wiring (through either the Inhabit or Outrage Arcanoi) a fire started, and the PC is lucky to have survived.<br /> <br /> 4) The vampire PC loses a prized retainer, ally, contact, etc. because a wraith possessed her and caused her death (the Puppetry Arcanos). Perhaps with a slow build up beforehand of the wraith making the vessel their consort.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=srVIPpMNYvE\" data-code=\"srVIPpMNYvE\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/srVIPpMNYvE/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> 5) When the vampire PC is listening to the radio at home or in a car, the wraith directly or indirectly threatens the PC. Maybe the NPR announcer's voice suddenly begins describing all the people the vampire controls through their influence and if they aren't smart they will lose all of them; or a commercial begins describing the estate sale of all the PCs property and possessions because they're recently deceased, or even an outright threat (Inhabit).<br /> <br /> 6) The wraith uses Pandemonium to perform subtle illusions to make the PC think they are being followed, or that another rival is observing them, etc.<br /> <br /> 7) And of course the blatant display of poltergeist phenomenon is an obvious way to grab their attention. Maybe not as dangerous to a vampire than to a mortal, but it should force them to take the wraith seriously.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nOR5l1NH8J0\" data-code=\"nOR5l1NH8J0\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/nOR5l1NH8J0/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Obviously certain defenses or wards used by the vampire could make one or more of these moot. But not everything can be warded or protected. Instead of a home or car radio, it is done while they are in an electronics store and the TVs in the display area starts being manipulated. Maybe it is not their prime haven that burns down, but a secondary haven. And so on.<br /> <br /> The issue is not to kill the PC, it is to teach him the lesson that wraiths can retaliate, and hopefully it will result in the PC wanting to make a deal that limits their actions to a reasonable course. And not all wraithly powers need to be exercise by one wraith. The wraith's friends, associates, or the political authorities can lend a hand.<br /> <br /> The important thing with any ghost story is atmosphere and mystery. You want to communicate with the player that they are dealing with the unknown, and let their own imagination conjure their fears of the unknown.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-20T12:00:34-08:00","id":1500186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1499965-ways-to-make-a-wraith-threatening?p=1500165#post1500165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> If you are looking for individual scenes that can get across to certain PCs that their powers do not make them immune, here are some examples of the kind of scenes I'd do.<br /> <br /> 1) Wraiths can invade your dreams and manipulate them (the Phantasm Arcanos). I would not go full Freddy Krueger, but I would use that as opportunity for wraiths to communicate to a vampire (who is slumbering in the daytime) in a safe environment for all sides. If you want to impress upon the vampire their power, you could have the Hierarchy hold a mock trial of the vampire for their crimes against wraiths. No powers are on either side can be used against each other, but you could show a lot of wraiths in a Star Chamber style court, wraiths in the jury, wraiths as bailiffs, etc. to showcase their numbers and resources. End the scene in a way that clearly (and hopefully ominously) warns the PC.<br /> <br /> 2) You can start the scene whenever the PC is driving somewhere. Describe that as they look in their rear view mirror they see someone smiling at them in their backseat. There is no one in the back seat of course, the mirror is simply showing the wraith (through the Embody Arcanos). If they turn their head and look back, they see nothing. But regardless their car suddenly jerks and it crashes (through either the Inhabit or Outrage Arcanoi).<br /> <br /> 3) When the vampire awakes, he finds out his haven is destroyed by a fire. Maybe he is in the basement and survived the flames. Maybe a retainer managed to move his resting spot to a new haven which he wakes up in. Maybe he awakens as the flames are erupting at sunset. But whether it is through some kind of spontaneous combustion or faulty wiring (through either the Inhabit or Outrage Arcanoi) a fire started, and the PC is lucky to have survived.<br /> <br /> 4) The vampire PC loses a prized retainer, ally, contact, etc. because a wraith possessed her and caused her death (the Puppetry Arcanos). Perhaps with a slow build up beforehand of the wraith making the vessel their consort.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=srVIPpMNYvE\" data-code=\"srVIPpMNYvE\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/srVIPpMNYvE/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> 5) When the vampire PC is listening to the radio at home or in a car, the wraith directly or indirectly threatens the PC. Maybe the NPR announcer's voice suddenly begins describing all the people the vampire controls through their influence and if they aren't smart they will lose all of them; or a commercial begins describing the estate sale of all the PCs property and possessions because they're recently deceased, or even an outright threat (Inhabit).<br /> <br /> 6) The wraith uses Pandemonium to perform subtle illusions to make the PC think they are being followed, or that another rival is observing them, etc.<br /> <br /> 7) And of course the blatant display of poltergeist phenomenon is an obvious way to grab their attention. Maybe not as dangerous to a vampire than to a mortal, but it should force them to take the wraith seriously.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nOR5l1NH8J0\" data-code=\"nOR5l1NH8J0\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/nOR5l1NH8J0/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Obviously certain defenses or wards used by the vampire could make one or more of these moot. But not everything can be warded or protected. Instead of a home or car radio, it is done while they are in an electronics store and the TVs in the display area starts being manipulated. Maybe it is not their prime haven that burns down, but a secondary haven. And so on.<br /> <br /> The issue is not to kill the PC, it is to teach him the lesson that wraiths can retaliate, and hopefully it will result in the PC wanting to make a deal that limits their actions to a reasonable course. And not all wraithly powers need to be exercise by one wraith. The wraith's friends, associates, or the political authorities can lend a hand.<br /> <br /> The important thing with any ghost story is atmosphere and mystery. You want to communicate with the player that they are dealing with the unknown, and let their own imagination conjure their fears of the unknown.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What a wonderful post! Thank you very much for the input!<br /> <br /> You got me scared with the video, I wasn't expecting that hahaha<br /> <br /> 1) This is really interesting, I like to play with my player's notion of what is real and what's not. It can lead to some very interesting situations when they don't know if they're dreaming or not, many times they try to check it somehow since the first time I did something like that, and it's a real boost to the atmosphere.<br /> <br /> 2) This one is a great classic, really cool and can work wonders with number 1 as well.<br /> <br /> 3) This one is surely good to make them feel that they're not safe (and make them angry lol).<br /> <br /> 4) The video you posted here really gave me a scare hahaha, this idea is always a good one, as even if the PC in question is &quot;tough&quot;, people who are important to them are not.<br /> <br /> 5) I could see the scene when you described it, that's really cool and horrifyingly funny as well.<br /> <br /> 6) This is one I often use through different means, one thing I always managed to accomplish is making my players paranoid lol, they're always thinking they're being followed or someone is hearing or even that they're going to be attacked anytime.<br /> <br /> 7) This one is a classic as well.<br /> <br /> You see, really great ideas from your post. I wouldn't kill them in any case (at least not at first <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />), but one thing you mentioned is almost always an issue in my current vampire game, the group has some Tremere allies, so they're many times safer than most through different rituals of protection etc, but as you mentioned, not everything can be warded or protected.<br /> I have to agree that atmosphere and mystery are probably the two most important things for this kind of story, and in the case of atmosphere, I'd say this is always one of the most important aspects of any given RPG, no matter the story. Thank you for the great input.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12348,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","user":"Herr Meister","date":". 12-20-2022, 03:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-20T12:17:37-08:00","id":1500187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1499965-ways-to-make-a-wraith-threatening?p=1500121#post1500121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a really interesting book that I definitely need to read. I have yet to read the book, but my impression is that an RPG Chronicle rarely fits into only one of these &quot;plots&quot; and I also wonder if Game of Thrones would be considered a Tragedy by this classification.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most RPG stories tend to switch from one to another over time, so they don't fit one category unless it is a one shot. Game of Thrones likewise changes categories depending on which aspect you focus on, but as an overall yeah, a Tragedy would fit it the best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-20T16:17:16-08:00","id":1500217,"title":"","content":"Wraiths (like most of the splats in cWoD) aren't really traditional folkloric ghosts. They're really OP due to sheer numbers and any group of Wraiths with Embody 5, along with the local Shroud level being really low, can manifest back into the Skinlands and just straight up fight you normally. Due to the very nature of most Vampires being secretive and death/jhor aspected, Vampire havens typically have very low Shroud levels.<br /> <br /> Unless you have any Necromancy Paths or some Blood Magic techniques to know when you're about to be ambushed, it'd be already too late.<br /> <br /> The most OP 5th level ability in World of Darkness (in my opinion), is Obliviate, which comes from Outrage level 5. With Obliviate, a Wraith can permanently send you to Oblivion with no possible counter, as each success with Obliviate gives you unsoakable Agg damage regardless of your splat.<br /> <br /> Wraits are underestimated and are unpopular compared to Mages and Werewolves, because nobody IRL wants to play a dead person (<b>EDIT</b>: Well in the case of Vampires, everyone wants to play them despite being dead.. because they're more &quot;smexy&quot;.. lol). And for most casual or semi-veteran cWoD players, Wraith is too hard to understand, just like Changeling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 12-20-2022, 07:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-20T18:05:04-08:00","id":1500235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1499965-ways-to-make-a-wraith-threatening?p=1500217#post1500217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wraiths (like most of the splats in cWoD) aren't really traditional folkloric ghosts. They're really OP due to sheer numbers and any group of Wraiths with Embody 5, along with the local Shroud level being really low, can manifest back into the Skinlands and just straight up fight you normally. Due to the very nature of most Vampires being secretive and death/jhor aspected, Vampire havens typically have very low Shroud levels.<br /> <br /> Unless you have any Necromancy Paths or some Blood Magic techniques to know when you're about to be ambushed, it'd be already too late.<br /> <br /> The most OP 5th level ability in World of Darkness (in my opinion), is Obliviate, which comes from Outrage level 5. With Obliviate, a Wraith can permanently send you to Oblivion with no possible counter, as each success with Obliviate gives you unsoakable Agg damage regardless of your splat.<br /> <br /> Wraits are underestimated and are unpopular compared to Mages and Werewolves, because nobody IRL wants to play a dead person (<b>EDIT</b>: Well in the case of Vampires, everyone wants to play them despite being dead.. because they're more &quot;smexy&quot;.. lol). And for most casual or semi-veteran cWoD players, Wraith is too hard to understand, just like Changeling.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically it's like the movie &quot;Poltergiest&quot; without the plot-armor that allows humans to survive. Imagine the powers you see in &quot;Poltergeist&quot; being directed with the ruthless efficiency of a player-character intent on murder.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-20T18:30:52-08:00","id":1500236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1499965-ways-to-make-a-wraith-threatening?p=1499984#post1499984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More importantly you have to remember that ghosts don't have the same daylight restriction that vampires do. <b>Thus a ghost can wander into any haven at mid-day and look around</b>. Now that might not sound like much of a threat, but consider how many things laying around your house that can be dangerous with only tiny amounts of manipulation. Starting fires, opening water taps, pulling back a window blind, etc can all be done, depending on the ghosts given load out. None of these things will directly harm a vampire, but it can create situations where the vampire is put in significantly greater danger.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not only that, even if you had multiple ghouls, they'd be unable to do anything to stop the Wraith (unless the Wraith decided to use Embody to cross back into the Skinlands). And starting a fire in a haven is definitely a sure-fire (pun intended) way to kill a Vampire; especially low humanity gen Vampires that cannot awaken very easily.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, Wraiths from the Hierarchy have weapon equipment made from Stygian Steel. Any weapon made from Stygian Steel inflicts aggravated damage instead of lethal. Unless your Vampire has Fortitude, a strike mission from the Hierarchy against them is basically a done deal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 12-20-2022, 09:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-21T12:15:20-08:00","id":1500322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1499965-ways-to-make-a-wraith-threatening?p=1500217#post1500217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wraiths (like most of the splats in cWoD) aren't really traditional folkloric ghosts. They're really OP due to sheer numbers and any group of Wraiths with Embody 5, along with the local Shroud level being really low, can manifest back into the Skinlands and just straight up fight you normally. </div> </div> </div> </div>While it has been quite a while since I dove into Wraith, I have this vague memory that mortals with a Willpower of five plus and a bad enough death situation were prerequisites to become a wraith, and even then, it wasn't automatic. How populous is the wraith community in a given city/location?<br /> <br /> I have had STs who rand cities as pretty much ghost free zones because of how rare willpower 5+ mortals are in general, which really messed with the necromancers in the group. On the other hand, having everyone who dies become a ghost kind of makes necromancers less transgressive and arcane and somewhat more akin to telemarketers trying to contact someone.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-21T13:43:24-08:00","id":1500332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1499965-ways-to-make-a-wraith-threatening?p=1500322#post1500322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How populous is the wraith community in a given city/location?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't believe there have ever been any rules or suggestions. Trying to figure out the demographics is tough because the wraith population of a Necropolis is not based on the current population of a city, but the legacy of its previous size throughout the time of its existence plus various migrations in and out and those who Trascend or fall to Oblivion. It all comes down to an individual STs tastes. <br /> <br /> However, given that there is a real economy, government, armed forces, public works, etc. there are far more ghosts than any other supernatural creature. I assume that in any given Necropolis there are many hundreds or thousands of wraiths and each Legion probably has anywhere from dozens to hundreds or even thousands of wraiths who are members (depending on the Legion) though relatively few are active Legionnaires plus a substantial number of thralls, drones, etc.<br /> <br /> Of course, if an ST wants a lower population of wraiths all she needs to do is reduce the number of Necropoli, concentrate them into regional capitals and make other cities mere outposts of the greater Necropolis they belong to. And of course there are plenty of small towns that would otherwise have no supernatural population except in special circumstances, but could easily have a dozen wraiths or more. Many small towns typically have one or more buildings said to be haunted.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-21T15:03:08-08:00","id":1500336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1499965-ways-to-make-a-wraith-threatening?p=1500322#post1500322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While it has been quite a while since I dove into Wraith, I have this vague memory that mortals with a Willpower of five plus and a bad enough death situation were prerequisites to become a wraith, and even then, it wasn't automatic. How populous is the wraith community in a given city/location?<br /> <br /> I have had STs who rand cities as pretty much ghost free zones because of how rare willpower 5+ mortals are in general, which really messed with the necromancers in the group. On the other hand, having everyone who dies become a ghost kind of makes necromancers less transgressive and arcane and somewhat more akin to telemarketers trying to contact someone.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> All you need to do to become a Wraith is have 5 Willpower at minimum, and since most Wraiths (discounting strange unknown entities that live in the Underworld) come from deceased humans, they definitely have more numbers than all of the splats in cWoD combined. And the Wraiths who don't get destroyed by Oblivion live on forever. Sure, 5 Willpower mortals are slightly uncommon, but they aren't really that rare.<br /> <br /> I'd even dare to think there are more Wraiths (+ Spectres; those who have been corrupted by Oblivion) than there are the living in cWoD. <br /> <br /> Also, I think Wraiths in general are actually more common than people think, considering the entire Underworld economy is driven by soulforging other Wraiths. The population of Wraiths in the Underworld may be artificially deflated due to the sheer fact of the institution of soulforging. If soulforging never became a thing or slowly fell out of favor, say, with Wraiths purely relaying on relics instead of soulforged material; then the Wraith population would be even larger in scale.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-21T21:51:38-08:00","id":1500355,"title":"","content":"Imagine having access to Auspex 5 as a rank Neonate, except it doesn't occupy your attention, takes no Willpower, and you can have multiple going at one time. <br /> <br /> Now imagine this ability has a sub ability that gives you pretty much blanket access to some of the most heinously irritating and annoying powers imaginable, and this power can act independently of you. Someone sneaking up on you? Whoops, they tripped! Someone got a gun to your head? Guess what malfunctioned as soon as they pull the trigger! Some scumbag got you down? Guess whose car no longer works, boss suddenly hates him, girlfriend suddenly leaves him, and apartment burns down! <br /> <br /> Wraiths are not &quot;threatening&quot; in the sense that a Brujah with 5 in Potence and Celerity and Burning Wrath is. They are threatening in the ways that Lady Luck is threatening, which is far, far worse.<br /> <br /> (V20 because You Already Know Why)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27252-hades","name":"Hades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-21T22:38:41-08:00","id":1500356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1499965-ways-to-make-a-wraith-threatening?p=1500186#post1500186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What a wonderful post! Thank you very much for the input!<br /> <br /> Thank you for the great input.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am glad it's been of help for you. Way back when I was very dismissive of Wraith as a game and a setting element, but a friend said a few things that had a lot of impact on me. Since then I've given a lot of thought to Wraith. And even though I must admit it will never be a fan favorite game since being a ghost has no power fantasy elements to players, I actually think it is the best done of all the WoD games.<br /> <br /> BTW, the Omen trilogy has a lot of elements that are absolutely terrifying and easily translated into Spectre activity. If wraiths can be frightening, then spectres can be absolutely terrifying (though they are even more limited by the Shroud than wraiths). <br /> <br /> If you can expand the normal Arcanoi with the &quot;forbidden&quot; Arcanoi and Dark Arcanoi, the ability of ghosts to deliver weird and scary effects expands greatly. I just find reading the Arcanoi description and thinking of things to do with them to lead to less frightening examples than to see great horror movies and translating what you say to those Arcanoi. It's just an example that the people without knowing the &quot;rules&quot; are more imaginative than than those who know them. The Wraith developers and writers really did a great job of translating actual folklore and cinematic tropes into game mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}